Build workflow report (0) {
## Dates and evidence

Report updated 2026-11-01. “Earlier” means already recorded by 2026-11-01; exact execution dates are unavailable in this checkout and are not inferred. Current experiments below ran on 2026-11-01. Historical target receipts are absent here; detailed prior contracts/results remain in `git show c48bb8a2:institute/anicca/Build.md`. Current receipts: `target/build-iteration/common-workflows/`.

The remaining user-selected tasks are in [Build.md](../../anicca/Build.md). This report records completed work and decisions, not permission to launch more experiments.

## Current working defaults

- Use one `nix develop .#interface` shell for a work session; run `cargo xtask` inside it and use `cargo check` for checks. Warnings are errors. Preserve caches and actual source/tool/feature invalidation.
- Keep pinned Rust 1.96/LLVM, local Linux Clang/Wild 0.9, automatic Cargo jobs, incremental dev compilation, line tables and Interface 256 codegen units. Shipping settings are separate.
- GitHub Actions has two platform workflows: Linux Lince with Park, and Android Lince. Automated Actions use compilation checks and requested optimized packages, without test suites. Local tests and performance experiments remain allowed. Linux Actions retains mold until the optimized Wild comparison qualifies a change; Android keeps its NDK linker and 16 KB alignment.
- Actions restores compatible Cargo libraries/metadata, registry archives and Git dependencies, then restores timestamps only for unchanged source bytes and permissions. Cache identity includes compiler, native libraries/tools, Rust flags, lockfile and build recipes. Application edits share the dependency cache rather than creating a large archive per commit; changed inputs still recompile. APKs, signing material and final executables are excluded. Android also caches cargo-ndk and Gradle dependencies.
- For Park protocol changes use `cargo xtask park protocol-check`. It currently passes 185 tests with two existing ignored cases. Native graphics, physical input and recovery need their relevant Park probes and acceptance checks; protocol tests do not replace them.
- For the four Store transaction targets use `cargo xtask test-store-transactions`: account, assertion, record and standing transactions; scoped SQLite optimization level 2 and four test threads. All 74 current cases pass. Native/shipping SQLite settings are unchanged.
- Keep scoped Store/Fiote/authoring dependencies, content-aware Anicca/native/icon caching and recovery, scanner pruning, PATH normalization and repository-root content discovery. Freedoom generation remains optional under `stuff`.
- Keep Engine-bound typed execution identity, pure Nucleus types, Store's fail-closed behavior and simulation's own-input guard. Complete effective-input provenance is still unfinished.
- Socket caching and nextest remain scoped options, not universal defaults. Nextest was validated for seven Store cases; its combination with the optimized four-target recipe is untested. Normal commands must not depend on missing scripts under `target`.
- `cargo xtask dev` uses release; Park session/protocol commands use development/test profiles. Do not infer release gains from dev-only timings or add independent percentages.

